{"case_id":"C057","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API protocol","configuration","input/output size semantics","encoder attack surface"],"confidence":96,"affected_functions":["BrotliEncoderCompress","BrotliDecoderDecompress"],"reason":"H0 exercises only the streaming decoder through BrotliDecoderDecompressStream. S1 explicitly includes the one-shot encoder BrotliEncoderCompress and one-shot decoder BrotliDecoderDecompress, whose buffer extents are coupled to input_size, encoded_size, and decoded_size. The encoder is wholly unexercised, including quality, lgwin, mode, output-capacity, and zero-capacity behavior; the one-shot decoder wrapper and its decoded-buffer capacity protocol are also absent.","evidence":["decode_fuzzer.c calls BrotliDecoderCreateInstance, BrotliDecoderDecompressStream, and BrotliDecoderDestroyInstance, but never calls BrotliDecoderDecompress or BrotliEncoderCompress.","build.sh builds and links brotlidec-static and libbrotlicommon-static, but does not build or link an encoder library.","S1 changes BrotliEncoderCompress parameters to input_buffer[BROTLI_ARRAY_PARAM(input_size)] and encoded_buffer[BROTLI_ARRAY_PARAM(*encoded_size)], directly identifying caller-controlled size/buffer relationships.","The visible BrotliEncoderCompress body reads out_size from *encoded_size and has an explicit out_size == 0 branch, exposing output-capacity semantics not covered by H0.","S1 likewise changes BrotliDecoderDecompress to relate encoded_buffer to encoded_size and decoded_buffer to *decoded_size, while H0 covers only the distinct streaming API."],"recommended_action":"Add a one-shot encoder target that derives quality, lgwin, mode, and output capacity from fuzz input and calls BrotliEncoderCompress, preferably validating successful output by decoding it. Also add direct BrotliDecoderDecompress coverage with varied decoded_size capacities, including zero and undersized buffers, while supplying storage consistent with the declared extents."}
